cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use mk2vsc or the file-format documentation in it, please cite it as below."
title: "mk2vsc: Victron VEConfigure .rvms/.rvsc configuration files without VEConfigure"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hart
    given-names: Kyle
version: 0.7.0
date-released: 2026-09-04
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/kylehart/mk2vsc"
url: "https://kylehart.github.io/mk2vsc/"
keywords:
  - Victron
  - VEConfigure
  - VE.Bus
  - MultiPlus
  - rvms
  - rvsc
  - file format
abstract: >-
  A zero-dependency Python library and command-line tool that reads, validates, decodes, diffs,
  edits and qualifies the .rvms configuration files produced by Victron VRM Remote VEConfigure,
  together with a written description of the file format: section grammar, per-section integrity
  checksum, the per-setting schema (scale, offset, default, min, max), the settings table with
  Victron's own names and identifiers, and the assistant area.
